# Prefer if / else and early exits; avoid switch

Use `if` / `else` with early exits (`return`, `continue`, `break` out of a loop) as much as possible, so the main path stays unindented. Do **not** use `switch` / `case` statements.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — switch
switch (status) {
  case "loading":
    return "Loading…";
  case "error":
    return error ?? "Something went wrong.";
  default:
    return "Ready";
}

// ✅ GOOD — early returns
if (status === "loading") return "Loading…";
if (status === "error") return error ?? "Something went wrong.";
return "Ready";
```

For a plain value-per-key mapping, a lookup object (`Record<Key, Value>`) is also fine.
